"The prognosis is influenced by several factors, including a preoperative PSA of 8.7 and an ISUP grade group 3 Gleason pattern on prostatectomy. Positive surgical margins are concerning findings. Conversely, the absence of seminal vesicle invasion and lymphovascular invasion are favorable elements. The biopsy history shows progression from Gleason 0+0 to Gleason 3+4 with perineural invasion noted at the second sampling site. Missing nodal sampling widens uncertainty regarding nodal status. Prognostic revision would be significantly aided by postoperative PSA levels and their subsequent trajectory, as this information is currently unknown. The fixed estimated horizon is 56.82 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 36.93–76.70 months; its coverage has not been validated."
